   "repo_name": "potpie-ai/potpie",
   "summary": "Community drive-by fix from fazalpsinfo-cmyk defaulting naive as_of values to UTC inside _parse_as_of_iso in the MCP inbound adapter; still open.",
   "description": "A small patch against the same naive-datetime crash as issue #1008, touching only `_parse_as_of_iso` in the MCP server so a date-only `as_of` comes back timezone-aware. It reproduces green against the reported MCP path, which is exactly why it is the cautionary case: RankingService.rank() still keeps a caller-supplied `now` as given and `_recency_score` still normalizes only `valid_at`, so the HTTP read surface, `--as-of` on the CLI and replay all remain exposed. Recorded as the verification evidence behind the failed boundary-only fix, with PR #1009 carrying the fuller normalization. Search terms: PR 1012, _parse_as_of_iso, timezone-aware as_of, boundary-only patch, naive datetime TypeError, incomplete fix."
