   "description": "Opened 2026-05-29 and merged 2026-06-03 by Bharath Kumar K. This is the web half of the `potpie login` CLI flow: the sign-in page accepts a `cli_callback` parameter, the browser Firebase session is exchanged for a backend-minted custom token, and that token is POSTed back to the CLI's local callback listener before app/(auth)/cli-success/page.tsx confirms the handoff to the user. New modules are lib/auth/cli-callback.ts, lib/auth/cli-callback-url.ts and lib/auth/cli-success.ts with tests alongside. State and nonce binding on the callback (commit 02d90db) prevents a malicious page from completing someone else's login — invalid or missing CLI callback state must not complete login. Only useful together with the companion potpie PR that starts the local callback server and stores credentials; the two shipped as a pair."
