   "description": "Domain-only validation of semantic mutation payloads: reads the ontology and contract constants, never a backend, so a payload can be checked without a store. Emits per-op structured issues (error / warning) plus a MutationRisk classification and a status of accepted / review_required / deferred / rejected; the batch decision is apply / review_required / rejected. A batch applies atomically — if any op cannot be auto-applied under the caller's approval flags the whole batch returns review_required and nothing is written. This is where 'evidence required for truth class', 'predicate not allowed between these labels' (allowed_pairs violations), unknown-label and missing-description findings originate."
