   "description": "Every claim is one :RELATES_TO edge between entities keyed by deterministic (group_id, entity_key). The edge carries the predicate as `name`, bitemporal validity (valid_at / invalid_at for event time, created_at / expired_at for system time), V1.5 claim metadata (truth, source_refs, claim_key), and the natural-language fact text the agent reads and the vector index embeds. The MERGE key includes source_ref so two distinct sources making the same claim land as two corroborating edges while a re-scan of the same source updates its edge idempotently in place. Validated end to end by pocs/position_b/poc.py including supersession, point-in-time queries, corroboration and native-vector semantic search. This is the file for 'why did my edge not supersede the old one' and for MERGE / randomUUID / dynamic SET e:Label questions."
