   "language": "python",
   "loc": 1494,
   "summary": "Single-agent ingestion loop that turns a batch of ContextEvents into graph mutations, checkpointed per tool call.",
   "description": "Backed by pydantic-deep (upstream vstorm-co/pydantic-deepagents). Receives a batch of recently-arrived ContextEvents for a pot and runs to completion against a tool surface of read-only graph lookups (context_search, context_timeline), a fat mutation tool (apply_graph_mutations), event-completion control (mark_events_processed / mark_event_processed) and a terminal finish_batch tool. Merges the matching EventPlaybooks into its run prompt so behavior is event-shaped. Progress is checkpointed after every tool call through AgentCheckpointStorePort so a worker crash mid-run resumes on a follow-up dispatch. This is where ingestion hangs, runaway tool loops, empty-mutation runs and 'the agent never called finish_batch' are diagnosed."
