   "description": "One formula serves every reader: readers extract the per-factor inputs (which are use-case specific) and RankingService applies the uniform product with a coverage-quality downweight. Semantic similarity carries the highest default weight because with embed-on-write plus ANN it is the primary recall signal. The module is deliberately I/O-free — callers build Candidate objects from graph reads and get back RankedItem objects with the full score breakdown attached so readers can explain rankings to the agent and so 'higher-strength wins, every time, deterministically' is testable. Grep here when results are ordered surprisingly or when tuning retrieval weights."
