   "language": "python",
   "loc": 401,
   "summary": "The only module importing opentelemetry; exports OTLP spans to the collector, provider-aware and fail-open.",
   "description": "Implements ObservabilityPort over OTLP to a collector (Tempo / Prometheus) and is the single opentelemetry import in the codebase, which is what keeps the backend swappable. Provider-aware: when a parent TracerProvider already exists (running inside the Potpie Celery worker where Logfire instruments pydantic-ai) it attaches an extra OTLP BatchSpanProcessor to the existing provider and never calls set_tracer_provider, so model and tool spans nest under our event spans automatically; standalone HTTP/CLI/MCP gets a fresh provider. Configured entirely through standard OTEL_* env such as OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT. If the observability extra is not installed or any setup step fails it degrades to a silent no-op — observability never fails the process."
