   "statement": "The six generic top-level packages (`domain`, `application`, `adapters`, `bootstrap`, `benchmarks`, `host`) move under `potpie/context-engine/src/potpie_context_engine/`, and no top-level compatibility shims are kept.",
   "rationale": "PR #1016 (nndn) argues the names were never API: 'Generic package names are collision-prone in any downstream environment, and the current import paths were never a declared API — freezing them by letting external consumers import the engine as-is would lock in accidents.' Shipping shims would ratify exactly the accidental surface the move exists to retire. `potpie_context_engine/api.py` pins the supported consumer surface instead (`GraphBackend`, `GraphPlanStorePort`, `GraphInboxStorePort`, `GraphService`).",
   "alternatives_rejected": "Deprecation shims re-exporting `domain.*`/`application.*` for a release — rejected per the plan decision that those names were never public API. Rewriting the RPC/telemetry capability vocabulary (`host.pots.use_managed`, `host.daemon.stop`, setup-step owner labels) was also explicitly rejected: those are wire/analytics names that only textually resemble module paths.",
