   "description": "Historical decision explaining why some older pots contain 256-dimension embeddings that today's 384-dimension vector index cannot reach, and why `graph repair --semantic-index` exists. The failure was silent: hashing-vector and semantic-vector mode reported identically in `graph status`, so users got poor recall with no signal. Search terms: hashing embedder, 256 dim embeddings, dimension mismatch, vector index rebuild, poor semantic recall, embedding migration."
