   "description": "adapters/outbound/event_stream/redis_publisher.py with inmemory_publisher.py as the local sibling, configured from REDIS_URL. It feeds GET /api/v1/context/events/{event_id}/stream and GET /api/v1/context/pots/{pot_id}/events/stream, which drive the live activity timeline and ingestion pipeline views in potpie-ui. The readiness check treats an unconfigured publisher as healthy, reporting 'not configured (NoOp)' — so a silent live timeline usually means NoOp, not an outage. Search: SSE not updating, live events stuck, redis pubsub, event fan-out, noop publisher."
