   "summary": "Overview of the five specialized prebuilt agents: Codebase Q&A, Unit Test, Integration Test, Debugging, and Code Changes.",
   "description": "The hub page for Potpie's suite of specialized prebuilt agents, each leveraging the code knowledge graph and code-analysis tools. It indexes five agents: the Codebase Q&A Agent (answers questions about functionality, architecture and structure, with `@function` entry-point references), the Unit Test Agent (test plans and unit test code for a given function or class), the Integration Test Agent (test plans from an entry-point function, best on Python/JavaScript/TypeScript), the Debugging with Knowledge Graph Agent (analyzes stacktraces and errors against your codebase, adds print debugging, iterates toward root cause), and the Code Changes Agent (analyzes the current branch against the default branch, identifies impacted APIs and cascading effects). Search this for 'which agent should I use', 'stacktrace agent', 'generate unit tests for my repo', 'which APIs does my change break'."
