   "url": "https://linear.app/potpie/issue/POT-1742",
   "summary": "Internal playbook for the recurring Vanta and Dependabot vulnerability sweeps across all eight potpie repos.",
   "description": "The internal procedure behind the steady stream of 'fixed high/med/critical vanta vulnerabilities' PRs that dominate potpie-workflows, pie and potpie-ui history. It defines the severity-to-SLA mapping, the order of operations (bump the direct constraint in pyproject.toml or package.json, regenerate uv.lock / pnpm-lock.yaml, re-run the test suite, never pin a transitive dependency in a lockfile alone), and the rule that a constraint added purely to block a transitive downgrade must be documented in the repo's SECURITY.md so the next engineer does not remove it as unused. It names the repeat offenders seen in practice — joserfc, h11/uvicorn, python-multipart, form-data, dompurify, js-yaml, protobufjs, websocket-driver and pyo3 in the Rust parsing extension — and assigns the sweep to the infra-security rotation. Tracked under Linear POT-1742."
