   "description": "Reading the potpie-workflows pull-request history, the dominant signal is dependency security, not feature delivery: of the last ~40 PRs, the large majority are titled some variant of 'fixed high/med/critical vanta vulnerabilities', '[Vanta] Fix High vulnerabilities in potpie-workflows', 'fix: patch CVE-2025-43859 — update h11 and uvicorn', 'fix: upgrade joserfc to remediate CVE-2026-48990' or 'chore(deps): bump python-multipart'. The actual product PRs are a thin band — specgen replaced with a two-phase deep agent, multi-batch structured Q&A, the plangen redesign, codegen changes — and they cluster around a handful of authors while the CVE stream is spread across shmbhvi101, Harigithub11, kshitij2040 and the cursor GitHub app. The practical consequence for anyone querying this repo's timeline: a naive 'what changed recently' read returns almost entirely dependency bumps and will mislead an agent about where the engineering effort actually went."
