   "description": "`potpie setup --repo . --agent claude` builds a `SetupPlan` covering config, storage, daemon, the active `default` pot, repo source registration and skill installation, and is safe to re-run. `--backend` picks the GraphBackend profile (default `falkordb_lite`), `--daemon`/`--in-process` selects host mode, `--dry-run` previews without executing, and `--scan` is an opt-in working-tree scan that is OFF by default — setup does not scan your repo unless asked. There is deliberately no separate manual ingest step: the CLI registers sources and the configured agent ingests when the task requires it. Search terms: potpie setup, first run, onboarding, wizard, uv tool install potpie, setup --dry-run, why is my pot empty after setup."
