   "summary": "type(scope): summary commit titles, with the POT-#### Linear id and the PR number appended.",
   "description": "The convention is visible across every repo's history: `fix(cli): add config list and no-key get for non-secret config inspection (#966)`, `feat(cli): source status no-ID summary and doctor effective repo pot (POT-1763 and POT-1779) (#929)`, `fix: remediate Vanta dependency CVEs and bump torch to 2.12.1 (#1000)`, `feat(demo): enable redis DLQ demo flow for all accounts`, `Fix include-family/graph-view vocabulary boundary (POT-1770) (#985)`. Linear team POT is the ticket namespace (POT-1397 through POT-1990 appear in real commit subjects). Scoped titles are what makes `git log --oneline` and Potpie's own change-timeline ingestion readable. Search terms: commit message format, conventional commits, PR title lint, POT ticket, changelog generation, squash merge title."
