   "description": "docs/context-graph/writing.md §3 states the rule precisely: 'A missing description is only a warning, never a reject — but recall depends on the agent-authored retrieval card, so skills treat it as mandatory'. The lowering tier derives summaries only from authored material via `compact_entity_summary`, so a bare re-reference never clobbers a stored summary but also never improves it. Thin descriptions are the single biggest cause of 'the graph has the fact but search does not find it'. Search terms: description quality, semantic search recall, embedding text, entity summary, retrieval card, graph quality low-confidence, orphan entities."
