   "description": "aks-potpie-prod is the `azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.potpie_aks` named `a0031-potpie-aks-prod` in resource group `a0031-potpie-aks-Resources-Prod`, region Central India, node pool `default` on Standard_D2s_v3, defined in potpie-terraform/terraform-azure/main.tf. Networking lives in `a0031-potpie-aks-Network-Prod` with `potpie-vnet`, an `aks-subnet` and `mgmt-subnet`, and NSG rules allowing HTTP/HTTPS plus internal traffic. The defining architectural choice here is that PostgreSQL was pulled out of Azure managed flexible-server and moved into the cluster as a Helm StatefulSet — `azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server`, its private DNS zone and the 5432 NSG rule were all deleted (see POSTGRESQL_MIGRATION.md). Storage uses the `azure-disk-premium` StorageClass (disk.csi.azure.com, Premium_LRS, WaitForFirstConsumer). Search for AKS, Central India, a0031-potpie-aks-prod, azure migration, azure-disk-premium or in-cluster postgres."
